A timer line armed for a deadline nearer than any other of its core's leaves the core's timer where it was.
The timer would interrupt after the deadline and the thread sleep past it;
the nearest deadline a core's timer wakes for comes no later than that of any timer line armed there.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: armed timer line comes due before the timer wakes for it

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -45,7 +45,6 @@ void irq_set_bits(struct irq *irq, uint32_t bits)
         struct core *core = core_self();
         irq->core = (uint8_t)core_index();
         if (tick_before(irq->deadline, core->nearest_deadline)) {
-            core->nearest_deadline = irq->deadline;
             core->wake_stale = true;
         }
     }
